# 09 — The Review Loop

> **For the agent reading this:** Read `plans/08-semantics-and-entities` first, especially its §14 (the starting sketch for this phase), and `plans/thinking-04-evals` (why being able to see the result matters, and where this is heading: evals and export). This phase lets both sides of the loop **see** the level, not just read it. It adds:
> - **shots:** a capture of the view, saved in the project with the camera that took it, so a shot is also a bookmark that can be revisited and taken again after the level changes. Every capture, the human's or the agent's, goes to one **Shots** panel;
> - **the Walk tool:** drop a first-person or third-person camera into the level and move through it at the player's eye height, to check sightlines. It's a camera, not a game: no physics and no collision, only **floor-follow** (the eye stays at player height above whatever is underneath);
> - **`render_view`:** the agent renders the scene (a plan, a contact sheet, a close-up, an eye view, a walk along a path, or a stored shot) and gets it back as an image, to check its own work;
> - **review habits** in the guide, and model sheets of the entities.
>
> The array tool is phase 10. Export to engines and the evals of `thinking-04` come later. The work is split into small increments (§9). Each one ends with the human ↔ agent loop still working and a browser checklist for Orlando. Add this phase's terms to `GLOSSARY.md` (marked "from 09") as they land. Log progress in a §12 at the end of this file, as 08 did.

